From c7286fb87de169803d1cd2223f3cbf424e0599bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 14:31:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mfd: stm32-lptimer: drop address and size cells
 requirement

The "#address-cells" and "#size-cells" properties are only meaningful
when the LPTIM instantiates an addressable child node. Among the LPTIM
sub-nodes, only the "trigger@N" node carries a "reg" property; the
"pwm", "counter" and "timer" children are not addressable.

Requiring these two properties unconditionally forces every LPTIM node
to declare them even when no addressable child is present, which is not
necessary and triggers following dtbs_check failures:
(st,stm32-lptimer): '#address-cells' is a required property
from schema $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/mfd/st,stm32-lptimer.yaml

Drop "#address-cells" and "#size-cells" from the required list. They stay
described as properties, and a child node carrying a "reg" without the
parent declaring the cells is already caught at build time by dtc, so no
valid configuration is left unchecked.

Fixes: b88091f5d84a ("dt-bindings: mfd: Convert stm32 low power timers bindings to json-schema")
Change-Id: I766cbefe6ee3a26f1193e0d8faf3da023ab0ccab
Signed-off-by: Olivier Moysan <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/568588
Domain-Review: Fabrice GASNIER <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Fabrice GASNIER <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/st,stm32-lptimer.yaml | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/st,stm32-lptimer.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/st,stm32-lptimer.yaml
@@ -133,8 +133,6 @@ patternProperties:
       - reg
 
 required:
-  - "#address-cells"
-  - "#size-cells"
   - compatible
   - reg
   - clocks
